{"id": "EUVD-2026-81872", "enisaUuid": "9a4eeb08-f41d-3801-8260-518f749542d2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid5: round bitmap stripes with sector division\n\nraid5_bitmap_sector_map() aligns the array range to full RAID5 stripe\nwidths before converting it to component sectors. That width is\nchunk_sectors multiplied by the number of data disks, and it is not\nalways a power of two.\n\nReproduce with a 4-disk RAID5, 1024-sector chunks, and three data disks.\nThe full-stripe width is 3072 sectors. For a one-sector write at array\nsector 3072, correct rounding gives array range [3072, 6144), which maps\nto component range [1024, 2048). The old round_down()/round_up() logic\ninstead gives [1024, 4096), which maps to [0, 1024).\n\nUse sector_div() based arithmetic so the rounded range is aligned to the\nactual RAID5 stripe width.\n\nThe deterministic mapper test now reports the fixed component range as\n[1024, 2048), while the old mask-based range was [0, 1024).", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d7490007707f90691911385365bd1d691d99225", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cab7d949b18b2f1cd625689dc16c5f81236bac93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02c10581866d08822c6348e299881485fc546185", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ccbdc483eb041eef809e9ff223d1ad63518a2c52", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17ea021ae74987d6064c8195c4922fa025753892"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3w3q-m725-w3pg", "CVE-2026-90279"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "295e09ab-0add-3054-ba43-0ccf399592ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa8e15d69f5c0044d5bff61844e163aacc4ac172 <cab7d949b18b2f1cd625689dc16c5f81236bac93"}, {"id": "2e034578-ab75-3815-bebc-bdda95162b03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "683e4e93-f918-3d71-8cce-28bb234fb591", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c89f604476cf15c31fbbdb043cff7fbf1dbe0cb <02c10581866d08822c6348e299881485fc546185"}, {"id": "6c8f21ca-ede1-3e22-a783-1fcd573c50ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c89f604476cf15c31fbbdb043cff7fbf1dbe0cb <ccbdc483eb041eef809e9ff223d1ad63518a2c52"}, {"id": "75cd4784-2d84-3948-b7d7-ac25a792e3c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c89f604476cf15c31fbbdb043cff7fbf1dbe0cb <17ea021ae74987d6064c8195c4922fa025753892"}, {"id": "8a7cafc9-7d28-3cdd-aa95-2a6e100fe7a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13.2 <6.14"}, {"id": "952f3b1c-7381-3542-acc7-6c77ec9b266a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.79 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "a1a15615-e956-3790-8392-e0998cd8e0de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a41a0df5d7638acf15e723ad985980b4f7ff9383"}, {"id": "b039a889-8848-3033-9c15-d2731677f612", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.13 <6.12.110"}, {"id": "b1e815e4-56f1-387d-b2af-e3aa10a6fb04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "becafd1a-3b4c-3465-88cf-485b51714565", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bfe1e68a-cfdc-383b-a670-871b44624955", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ca643978-c178-3fbc-83be-48df4714c037", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e6bf5b9d-3f4c-3b79-af34-d96abccf18ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b29e6400be51c214a0ad30dce937348b57abe33a <9d7490007707f90691911385365bd1d691d99225"}, {"id": "f12e3760-0cfb-32ef-b062-d7194e2540c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "fdbd5f8e-a404-33c6-9cfd-34b4d7cf217c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b18f1e29-6dc3-3065-a8e1-42202562cbea", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}